<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Feb M3 money supply grows 15.82 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Feb M3 money supply grows 15.82 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 15.82 percent in February, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>January M3 growth was revised to 16.80 percent from a preliminary 16.89 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 17.34 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 17.06 percent in January.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economist forecast M3 year-on-year growth of 15.1 percent while private credit was seen expanding 16.39 percent.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>Feb 1997 preliminary M3 growth -- 15.82 percent</p>
<p>Feb 1997 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 17.34 percent</p>
<p>					   Jan '97	  Dec '96</p>
<p>M3  revised			    16.80	    13.61</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  19.09	    15.75</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  32.15	    30.90</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     17.06	    16.08</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (rand billions)</p>
<p>			    Feb '97(prel) Jan '97 (rev)  Dec '96 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	   327.42	  319.35	   319.43</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.    327.21	  325.67	   317.08</p>
<p>Private sector credit 379.49	  372.92	   367.01</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>			     16.62	   21.24	     --</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
